{
 "about": "How the printed rows and columns of the credit-institution templates (Annex VI to Delegated Regulation (EU) 2021/2178, every version in data/reference/regspec/bank_taxonomy) are read into facts. A row's label chain ('parent > child') is read segment by segment and the fragments combine; so is a column's header chain. Every row and column of every adopted version must resolve (tests/unit/test_taxonomy_vocabulary.py). A fragment with 'input' is a figure the institution enters itself (the platform holds no facts for it); the reason is shown on the form. Segments are matched after whitespace, dash and quote normalisation.",
